 "transcript": {
  "answer": "The advertised standard variable owner-occupier rate was **8.77%** in September 2026, while the RBA cash rate target (monthly average) was **4.36%**. That puts the home loan rate **4.41 percentage points** above the cash rate.\n\nThe gap has been roughly stable recently. In November 2025 it was 8.02% against 3.60%, a gap of 4.42 points. In January 2025 it was 8.77% against 4.35%, also 4.42 points.\n\nThese are advertised rates. Rates actually paid on new loans are lower, and the RBA publishes those in table F6.",
